id: genetic-focus-glass
name: Genetic Focus: Glass
order: 7
category: body
# "[Uncanny Monster]": it replaces that Primary Racial Trait - which, the table's. (1) Its Prerequisite, the Glass Genes Factor Trait,
# shown and never enforced.
importance: primary
# Its own description was given cut short ("T"): asked for.
text: >
  Genetic Focus: Glass (Body) [Uncanny Monster]:
  (1)-[Prerequisite]: Glass Genes Factor Trait.
  (2)-[Passive]: Halve your Soak Value.
  (3)-[Passive]: Gain Damage Reduction equal to your Soak Value.
  (4)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you use a Signature Technique, you may apply the Multi-Profile Super Profile to that Attacking Maneuver. If you do, you must select the Glass Profile for the effects of Multi-Profile, and you must trigger the 5th effect of Glass Genes on this Attacking Maneuver (if you have 2+ Adaptation Points).
  (5)-[Triggered/Start of Turn]: Spend 3 Adaptation Points to enter the Surging State until the end of your turn.
---

[passive]
# (2), (3) Body of Glass's words: the Soak Value halved, and as much Damage Reduction (actor-character.mjs).
soakValue *= 0.5;
allow damageReduction.soak;
# (4) A Signature Technique declared: Multi-Profile with the Glass Profile, asked, once a Round - Unique Technique's way; with 2+ Adaptation
# Points, Glass Genes (5) with it, the 2 spent for its Energy Charge (use-maneuver.mjs glassFocusMulti). Its attack's alone: no button.
allow focusGlass.multi;

# (5) Your turn begins with 3 Adaptation Points: Surging till the end of it. It spends: no Triggered/Automatic button, ticked on the turn's
# card (the user's).
[triggered/start-of-turn, chosen, effect 5]
requires stacksAtLeast(3, "adaptation");
adaptation.stacks -= 3;
enterState(surging, 1, turn);
